 "notes": {
  "forAnalyst": "Product, category and search queries for a storefront — the read side of the catalogue, shaped for a page rather than for a table.",
  "forArchitect": "Eight schema builders over Catalog, and the module that makes a catalog-read Cell possible: it declares three optional dependencies, so it can be deployed without pricing, inventory or marketing and simply returns less. Reads go to the index, not the catalog tables.",
  "forDeveloper": "Extend `ProductType` and the search query through the factory to add solution fields. Watch the N+1: resolve child collections through DataLoader, and remember a reindex is what makes new fields visible.",
  "owns": [],
  "reachForItWhen": [
   "A storefront, app or agent needs data shaped for one round trip",
   "You are extending an existing query or mutation rather than adding an endpoint",
   "The host should serve only this capability's API surface"
  ],
  "doNotReachForItWhen": [
   "Back-office CRUD — that is the module's REST controller",
   "You need a table: these modules own no schema, they compose other modules' services",
   "Bulk writes: a mutation per row is slower than the owning module's import path"
  ]
 },
